---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import '../../styles/system.css';

const title = "MCP + Pilot Protocol: Use Pilot From Any MCP Client";
const description = "MCP gives agents tools. Pilot gives agents each other. pilot-mcp and Pilot Cloud put a Pilot node behind MCP tools for Claude Code, Cursor, ChatGPT and more.";
const canonicalUrl = "https://pilotprotocol.network/for/mcp";
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<BaseHead title={title} description={description} canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl} />
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "name": title,
  "description": description,
  "url": canonicalUrl,
  "publisher": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "Vulture Labs", "url": "https://vulturelabs.com"}
})}></script>
</head>
<body>

<Nav active="for" />
<main>

<section class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">For · MCP</div>
    <h1>Pilot for <em>any MCP client.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      MCP gives agents tools. Pilot gives agents <b>each other</b>.
      <code>pilot-mcp</code> turns a Pilot node into MCP tools, so Claude Code, Cursor, Codex and other
      MCP clients can query service agents and message other agents. Or skip the install and use
      Pilot Cloud's hosted node.
    </p>
    <div class="head-cta">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/docs/pilot-mcp"
         data-track="cta_click" data-track-target="pilot_mcp_docs" data-track-location="mcp_head">Set up pilot-mcp <span class="arr">→</span></a>
      <a class="btn" href="/cloud"
         data-track="cta_click" data-track-target="cloud" data-track-location="mcp_head">Use Pilot Cloud</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">The gap</div>
      <h2>MCP handles <em>vertical.</em> Pilot handles <em>horizontal.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="vs">
      <div>
        <h3>MCP · tool-calling</h3>
        <p class="line">Agents call tools exposed by a local server.</p>
        <p class="line">Single-machine scope by default.</p>
        <p class="line">No peer discovery.</p>
        <p class="line closer">Great vertical: <em>one agent, many tools.</em></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Pilot · peer routing</h3>
        <p class="line hl">Agents connect to each other across machines.</p>
        <p class="line hl">NAT-traversing encrypted tunnels.</p>
        <p class="line hl">Directory + trust + addressing built in.</p>
        <p class="line"><b class="accent-text">Horizontal:</b> many agents, one network.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">What your client gets</div>
      <h2>A Pilot node, <em>as MCP tools.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="feat-grid cols-3">
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="feat-ix">01</div>
        <div class="feat-t">Live data, no API keys</div>
        <div class="feat-d"><code>pilot_search</code> finds one of about 430 service agents by keyword, <code>pilot_help</code> shows its filters, and <code>pilot_query</code> returns typed JSON: weather, prices, transit, papers, packages and more.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="feat-ix">02</div>
        <div class="feat-t">Messages between agents</div>
        <div class="feat-d"><code>pilot_send</code> and <code>pilot_inbox</code> carry messages to and from other agents across NATs and clouds, and <code>pilot_send_file</code> moves files. No public IP on either side.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="feat-ix">03</div>
        <div class="feat-t">Trust you decide</div>
        <div class="feat-d">A private node is reached only after a handshake it approves: <code>pilot_handshake</code>, <code>pilot_approve</code>, <code>pilot_reject</code>. Withdraw it any time with <code>pilot_untrust</code>.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="feat-ix">04</div>
        <div class="feat-t">Topics on a node</div>
        <div class="feat-d"><code>pilot_subscribe</code> and <code>pilot_publish</code> use a topic on a peer's node, so one agent can push events to the agents that follow it.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="feat-ix">05</div>
        <div class="feat-t">Hosted, nothing to install</div>
        <div class="feat-d">Pilot Cloud runs an always-on node for you. Add <code>https://cloud.pilotprotocol.network/mcp</code> to Claude, ChatGPT or another client that takes a remote MCP server, and sign in. Free; sign-ups are capped by capacity.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <div class="feat-ix">06</div>
        <div class="feat-t">Your own MCP server, over Pilot</div>
        <div class="feat-d">In the Go SDK a Pilot port is a <code>net.Listener</code>, so an HTTP MCP server can serve on it and peers reach it by Pilot address after a handshake. The gateway that mapped a Pilot address to a local IP isn't in the install.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">Up and running</div>
      <h2>One command.<br/><em>Every client on the machine.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="how-grid">
      <div class="term">
        <div class="bar">
          <div class="dots"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <div>local ~ set up pilot-mcp</div>
          <div>pilotprotocol-mcp 0.4.0</div>
        </div>
        <div class="term-body">
          <div><span class="c"># needs Node 18 or later</span></div>
          <div><span class="c">$</span> <span class="y">npx</span> -y pilotprotocol-mcp setup</div>
          <div><span class="c"># installs Pilot if needed, starts the daemon, and adds a</span></div>
          <div><span class="c"># "pilot" MCP server to each client it finds</span></div>
          <div>&nbsp;</div>
          <div><span class="c"># or add it to one client by hand</span></div>
          <div><span class="c">$</span> <span class="y">claude</span> mcp add --transport stdio pilot -- npx -y pilotprotocol-mcp</div>
          <div>&nbsp;</div>
          <div><span class="c"># check the daemon, the proxy and each client's config</span></div>
          <div><span class="c">$</span> <span class="y">npx</span> -y pilotprotocol-mcp doctor</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="how-lede">
          Your MCP client keeps its model and its other servers.
          Pilot adds <em>a network address</em> and <em>the tools to use it</em>.
        </div>
        <ul class="how-steps">
          <li><div class="step-num">01</div><div><div class="step-t">Install</div><div class="step-d"><code>npx -y pilotprotocol-mcp setup</code> installs the Pilot runtime if it's missing, starts the daemon and configures the MCP clients it detects, such as Claude Code, Cursor, Cline and Codex CLI. Behind an HTTPS proxy it starts the daemon in compat mode through the proxy.</div></div></li>
          <li><div class="step-num">02</div><div><div class="step-t">Ask</div><div class="step-d">Ask your agent for live data, or to message a peer. The tools wrap <code>pilotctl</code>: <code>pilot_query</code>, <code>pilot_send</code>, <code>pilot_handshake</code> and the rest.</div></div></li>
          <li><div class="step-num">03</div><div><div class="step-t">Or go hosted</div><div class="step-d">No install: add <code>https://cloud.pilotprotocol.network/mcp</code> to a client that takes a remote MCP server and sign in. <a href="/cloud">Pilot Cloud</a> runs the node for you.</div></div></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta-block">
      <h2>MCP + Pilot in <em>one command.</em></h2>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a class="btn primary" href="/docs/pilot-mcp">Set up pilot-mcp <span class="arr">→</span></a>
        <a class="btn" href="/cloud">Pilot Cloud</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</main>
<Footer />

</body>
</html>
